    "id": "character-u+4e4b",
    "character": "之",
    "unicode": "U+4E4B",
    "title_english": "之 — movement, deixis, and grammatical extension",
    "summary_english": "The early graph depicts forward movement from a place. Qin forms divide into the lines that later yield 㞢 and 之, while the lexical history expands from ‘to go’ into deictic, pronominal, and attributive uses.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "之",
      "pronunciation": "zhī章纽、之部；章纽、之韵、止而切。",
      "bibliography": [
        "《汉语字形表》233页",
        "《郭店》96页",
        "《包山》91页",
        "《篆隶表》401页",
        "《睡甲》91页",
        "《说文》127页",
        "《玉篇之部》"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "会意字。商代文字从\n（止，像足形。参见止部“止”字条）\n﹑从󲴲\n（代表某地）\n，形向前，表示人离此地往他处而去。所从“止”旁，后讹变为“屮”。秦代文字有两种写法：一作\n（字形8）\n﹑󵚇\n（字形10）\n，后演变为楷书“㞢”\n（今仅见于偏旁，如“蚩”从虫﹑㞢声）\n；一作\n（字形9）\n，后演变为楷书“之”。本义是往，到……去。\n《尔雅·释诂上》：“之，往也。”\n《诗·卫风·伯兮》：“自伯之东，首如飞蓬。”\n《战国策·赵策三》：“齐闵王将之鲁。”\n引申为至。\n《诗·鄘风·柏舟》：“之死矢靡它。”\n（矢：通“誓”。靡它：没有别的心思）\n“之”多用于假借义，较常见的有：1.指示代词，相当于“这”。\n《诗·邶风·燕燕》：“之子于归，远送于野。”\n《庄子·逍遥游》：“之二虫又何知？”\n2.第三人称代词，相当于“他\n（她﹑它）\n”。\n《诗·周南·关雎》：“窈窕淑女，寤寐求之。”\n《荀子·天论》：“从天而颂之，孰与制天命而用之？”\n3.助词，相当于“的”。\n《诗·召南·何彼秾矣》：“平王之孙，齐侯之子。”\n《韩非子·难一》：“以子之矛，陷子之盾，何如？”\n（冀小军）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "explanation_english": [
        "An associative compound. The Shang graph combines 止, a pictograph of a foot, with 󲴲, which marks a place. The forward-facing foot depicts a person leaving this place and proceeding elsewhere. The 止 component was later reshaped as 屮.",
        "Qin writing preserves two formal lines. One line, represented by forms 8 and 10 in the source plate, developed into the regular-script form 㞢; it now survives chiefly as a component, as in 蚩, analysed as 从虫、㞢声. The other line, form 9 in the source plate, developed into regular-script 之.",
        "The primary meaning is ‘to go; to proceed to a place’. 《尔雅·释诂上》：“之，往也。” 《诗·卫风·伯兮》：“自伯之东，首如飞蓬。” 《战国策·赵策三》：“齐闵王将之鲁。”",
        "A derived sense is ‘to reach; unto’. 《诗·鄘风·柏舟》：“之死矢靡它。” The source notes that 矢 is used for 誓 here, and 靡它 means having no other attachment.",
        "Many frequent functions arose through phonetic borrowing. As a demonstrative pronoun it means ‘this’: 《诗·邶风·燕燕》：“之子于归，远送于野。” 《庄子·逍遥游》：“之二虫又何知？”",
        "As a third-person pronoun it refers to him, her, it, or them: 《诗·周南·关雎》：“窈窕淑女，寤寐求之。” 《荀子·天论》：“从天而颂之，孰与制天命而用之？”",
        "As a particle it marks attribution or possession, conventionally comparable to modern 的: 《诗·召南·何彼秾矣》：“平王之孙，齐侯之子。” 《韩非子·难一》：“以子之矛，陷子之盾，何如？” The entry is signed 冀小军. Images from the dictionary entry are intentionally omitted."
      ]
    },
